<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">French Louisiana</h1><p class="st-meta">1682 CE – 1762 CE · capital New Orleans</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">France's colony in the Mississippi basin, founded around the Gulf coast and New Orleans, whose Creole culture still marks the state of Louisiana.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1682 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rene-robert-cavelier-sieur-de-la-salle">René-Robert Cavelier de La Salle</a> travelled down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> and claimed its basin for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>, naming it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>. Settlement began when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-le-moyne-diberville">Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-maurepas">Fort Maurepas</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biloxi">Biloxi</a> in 1699. Mobile followed in 1702, and in 1718 his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-le-moyne-de-bienville">Bienville</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a>, the capital from 1722.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-law">John Law's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-company">Company of the Indies</a> ran the colony from 1717 to 1731, promoting settlement in a speculative boom that collapsed in 1720. Thousands of enslaved Africans were brought, mostly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegambia">Senegambia</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/code-noir">Code Noir</a> of 1724 governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> stretched in claim to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois-country">Illinois Country</a> and depended on Native alliances, though wars with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/natchez-chiefdom">Natchez chiefdom</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chickasaw-nation">Chickasaw Nation</a> were costly. It became a crown colony in 1731.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Facing defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years War</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> secretly ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> and the land west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1762, creating <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-louisiana">Spanish Louisiana</a>, while the eastern lands went to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> in 1763.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/french-louisiana.jpg" alt="French Louisiana" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Oren neu dag · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_flag_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1682 CE – 1762 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>New Orleans</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jean-Baptiste Le Moyne de Bienville, Pierre de Rigaud de Vaudreuil, Louis Billouart de Kerlérec</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Louisiana (New France), La Louisiane</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1722&amp;focus=french-louisiana" aria-label="French Louisiana on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2339 1083 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where French Louisiana lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2659 1339L2643 1286M2659 1339L3327 789M2659 1339L5054 728M2659 1339L2659 1339"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M